WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.561
Mary ran so fast that she was out of breath when she reached her rooms.

2
00:00:20.101 --> 00:00:20.981
Martha was waiting.

3
00:00:21.001 --> 00:00:24.062
"You're late," she told Mary.

4
00:00:24.082 --> 00:00:25.563
"Where have you been?"

5
00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:27.963
"I've seen Dickon!"

6
00:00:28.544 --> 00:00:29.404
Mary exclaimed.

7
00:00:30.984 --> 00:00:35.148
Martha wanted to know all about the garden tools and seeds that he had brought.

8
00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:38.651
"Did you ask someone where you might plant the seeds?"

9
00:00:39.892 --> 00:00:43.075
Mary was afraid to reveal anything about the secret garden.

10
00:00:43.095 --> 00:00:47.779
"I haven't asked anybody yet," she said hesitantly.

11
00:00:47.799 --> 00:00:52.143
"Well, I wouldn't ask the head gardener, Mr.

12
00:00:52.243 --> 00:00:54.144
Roach. He's a bit haughty.

13
00:00:55.245 --> 00:00:58.048
I'd ask Ben Weatherstaff, who's kinder than he looks.

14
00:00:59.252 --> 00:01:02.953
Mr. Craven lets him do what he likes because he was here when Mrs.

15
00:01:03.013 --> 00:01:04.053
Craven was alive.

16
00:01:05.154 --> 00:01:07.714
He used to make her laugh, and she liked him.

17
00:01:08.815 --> 00:01:11.055
Perhaps he'd find you a corner somewhere."

18
00:01:12.596 --> 00:01:13.956
Mary ate lunch quickly.

19
00:01:14.476 --> 00:01:17.477
She was eager to go back to working in the secret garden with Dickon.

20
00:01:18.697 --> 00:01:23.078
She hopped up from the table and was about to run outside, when Martha stopped her.

21
00:01:23.098 --> 00:01:25.759
"I've got something to tell you.

22
00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:30.277
Mr. Craven came back this morning, and he wants to see you."

23
00:01:31.838 --> 00:01:32.918
Mary turned pale.

24
00:01:32.938 --> 00:01:34.219
"Oh, why?

25
00:01:34.779 --> 00:01:36.881
He didn't want to see me when I first came."

26
00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:43.844
"Mrs. Medlock says it's because Mother met him when she was walking to Thwaite village," said Martha.

27
00:01:43.864 --> 00:01:47.947
"She'd never spoken to him before, but Mrs.

28
00:01:48.027 --> 00:01:50.548
Craven had been to our cottage two or three times.

29
00:01:52.149 --> 00:01:56.371
I don't know what Mother said to him, but he wants to see you before he goes away

30
00:01:56.431 --> 00:01:57.252
again tomorrow."

31
00:01:58.472 --> 00:01:59.853
"Oh!" cried Mary.

32
00:01:59.873 --> 00:02:02.113
"I'm so glad he's going away again."

33
00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:05.514
"He may not come back until autumn or winter.

34
00:02:06.635 --> 00:02:09.415
He's going to be traveling to several different places."

35
00:02:11.076 --> 00:02:11.496
If Mr.

36
00:02:11.536 --> 00:02:16.598
Craven didn't come back until autumn or winter, there would be time to watch the secret garden come

37
00:02:16.658 --> 00:02:22.780
alive. "Even if he finds out then and takes it away from me," Mary thought, "I will at

38
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:23.940
least have had that much."

39
00:02:25.252 --> 00:02:27.333
Suddenly the door opened, and Mrs.

40
00:02:27.393 --> 00:02:28.794
Medlock stepped into the room.

41
00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:34.716
"Go brush your hair, and get into your best dress," she said to Mary.

42
00:02:34.736 --> 00:02:38.598
"Mr. Craven sent me to bring you to his study."

43
00:02:39.778 --> 00:02:45.461
Mary's heart began to thump, and she felt herself changing into a stiff, plain child again.

44
00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:48.982
She said nothing while Martha helped her get dressed.

45
00:02:50.183 --> 00:02:51.063
She followed Mrs.

46
00:02:51.123 --> 00:02:53.124
Medlock silently down the corridors.

47
00:02:54.368 --> 00:02:55.549
What was there for her to say?

48
00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:57.210
She had to go see Mr.

49
00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:59.492
Craven. Mrs.

50
00:02:59.552 --> 00:03:01.633
Medlock took her to a new part of the house.

51
00:03:02.854 --> 00:03:05.256
A man sat in an armchair near the fire.

52
00:03:06.397 --> 00:03:10.800
He was not so much a hunchback as a man with high, crooked shoulders.

53
00:03:12.061 --> 00:03:12.941
He dismissed Mrs.

54
00:03:13.001 --> 00:03:14.823
Medlock before he spoke to Mary.

55
00:03:14.843 --> 00:03:16.704
"Are you well?"

56
00:03:17.184 --> 00:03:17.745
he asked.

57
00:03:17.765 --> 00:03:19.426
"Do they take good care of you?"

58
00:03:19.446 --> 00:03:22.128
"Yes," she answered.

59
00:03:23.572 --> 00:03:26.454
His black eyes seemed as if they scarcely saw her.

60
00:03:27.535 --> 00:03:29.437
His black hair was streaked with white.

61
00:03:30.618 --> 00:03:33.480
He would have been handsome if he had not looked so miserable.

62
00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:36.863
"I forgot about you," said Mr.

63
00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:40.546
Craven. "I meant to send you a nurse or a governess."

64
00:03:40.566 --> 00:03:47.151
"Please Mary could hardly speak because of the lump in her throat.

65
00:03:47.171 --> 00:03:52.756
"Please I'm too old for a nurse and I don't need a governess."

66
00:03:53.976 --> 00:03:57.318
"That's what that Sowerby woman said," he muttered to himself.

67
00:03:57.338 --> 00:03:59.739
"Is that Martha's mother?

68
00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:01.540
She knows all about children.

69
00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:02.761
She has 12."

70
00:04:02.781 --> 00:04:05.202
"What do you want to do?"

71
00:04:05.222 --> 00:04:07.623
"I want to play outdoors.

72
00:04:08.224 --> 00:04:10.665
It makes me hungry, and I'm getting stronger."

73
00:04:11.766 --> 00:04:13.327
Mary tried to sound brave.

74
00:04:13.347 --> 00:04:15.808
"I run and skip everywhere."

75
00:04:16.969 --> 00:04:18.169
"Don't look so frightened.

76
00:04:18.649 --> 00:04:19.670
You may do what you like.

77
00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.892
Do you want toys, books, dolls?"

78
00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:25.845
"Might I have a bit of dirt?"

79
00:04:26.985 --> 00:04:29.866
Mr. Craven looked startled at this strange request.

80
00:04:29.886 --> 00:04:34.388
"Dirt?" "To plant seeds in, to watch the plants grow.

81
00:04:35.329 --> 00:04:37.249
I didn't really know about gardens in India.

82
00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:42.091
I sometimes played at sticking flowers in the ground, but here it's different."

83
00:04:43.472 --> 00:04:46.933
Mr. Craven got up and began to walk slowly around the room.

84
00:04:48.634 --> 00:04:52.596
When he stopped and looked at her, his eyes seemed almost kind.

85
00:04:53.804 --> 00:04:55.845
"You may have as much dirt as you want.

86
00:04:57.005 --> 00:05:00.307
You remind me of someone else who loved the earth and things that grow.

87
00:05:01.427 --> 00:05:07.790
When you see a bit of dirt you want"—and here he almost smiled—"take it, child, and make it

88
00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:08.490
come alive.

89
00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:09.931
Now you must go."

90
00:05:12.032 --> 00:05:12.952
He summoned Mrs.

91
00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:16.994
Medlock, who led Mary down the corridors and left her at her rooms.

92
00:05:17.014 --> 00:05:19.475
"I can have my garden!"

93
00:05:19.975 --> 00:05:22.336
Mary said to herself as she ran outside.

94
00:05:23.568 --> 00:05:26.932
When she opened the door to the secret garden, Dickon was gone.

95
00:05:28.313 --> 00:05:33.539
But she found a note: a picture of a bird on a nest with the words "I will

96
00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:34.140
come back."
